        "original_id": "33092859-b35d-581e-9a84-e5bda15cdfee",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- People: Al-Ghazali, Ibn Rushd\n- Roles: theologian, jurist, philosopher, mystic, polymath\n- Places: Persia, al-Andalus, Western medieval world\n\nFacts:\n- Al-Ghazali, born in 1058 and deceased on 19 December 1111, was Abū Ḥāmid Muḥammad ibn Muḥammad al-Ghazālī.\n- Al-Ghazali was a Persian theologian, jurist, philosopher, and mystic.\n- Al-Ghazali was shortened as Al-Ghazali in Arabic and Ghazali in Persian, and he was known in the Western medieval world as Algazelus or Algazel.\n- Ibn Rushd, born on 14 April 1126 and deceased on 10 December 1198, was Abū l-Walīd Muḥammad Ibn Aḥmad Ibn Rushd.\n- Ibn Rushd was often Latinized as Averroes.\n- Ibn Rushd was a medieval Andalusian polymath.",
        "type": "TextSummary"
      },
